      ⍝ dyadic, B is 0 0 ----------------------------------

      )ERASE FN
∇FN
                        ⍝ OUTPUT   COMMENT
 'HELLO' ⎕ES 0 0        ⍝          Resets ⎕EM and ⎕ET
 ⎕ET                    ⍝ 0 0
                        ⍝
 '2+3' ⎕EA 'A←B)←2)'    ⍝ 5        Causes a syntax error
 ⎕ET                    ⍝ 2 2      Reports 2 2 as the event type
                        ⍝
 'WORLD'⎕ES 0 0         ⍝          Resets ⎕EM and ⎕ET
 ⎕ET                    ⍝ 0 0      Shows ⎕ET reset to 0 0
 'DONE'                 ⍝ DONE
∇

      FN
0 0
5
0 0
0 0
DONE

      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #29, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ ⎕ES's LRM-recommended idiom (Figure 40, p.353) for giving a
      ⍝ defined function a VALENCE ERROR when called with the wrong
      ⍝ number of arguments -- ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 1 -- used to fail when Y
      ⍝ (the declared but, in a monadic call, unsupplied left argument)
      ⍝ was still reachable from UserFunction::set_locked_error_info():
      ⍝ it unconditionally called Symbol::get_apl_value() on Y, which
      ⍝ throws VALUE ERROR for an unbound symbol, silently replacing the
      ⍝ intended ⎕ES-simulated error.
      ⍝
      )ERASE ROUND2
∇Z←Y ROUND2 X
 ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 1  ⍝SIGNAL VALENCE ERROR
 Z←(10*-Y)×⌊.5+X×10*Y
∇

      3 ROUND2 4.5677887
4.568

      ROUND2 4.5677887
VALENCE ERROR
      ROUND2 4.5677887
      ^              ^

      ⎕ET
5 1

      →

      )ERASE ROUND3
∇Z←Y ROUND3 X
 ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 4  ⍝SIGNAL DOMAIN ERROR
 Z←X
∇

      ROUND3 4.5677887
DOMAIN ERROR
      ROUND3 4.5677887
      ^              ^

      ⎕ET
5 4

      →

      ]EXPECT 1

